  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "The current best (config_031: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.725) is built on multiprofile aggregation. All 6 completed experiments use multiprofile, so the profile setting is unexplored. config_043 tests whether a singleprofile architecture with the same top-performing encoders (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l) and fusion (weighted) can match or exceed the multiprofile+transformer pipeline. This is a high-value uncertainty-reduction experiment: if singleprofile is competitive, it opens a cheaper, simpler path for the remaining 3 experiments; if it underperforms, it strongly confirms that multiprofile+transformer aggregation is essential, allowing us to focus remaining budget on fine-tuning within that family. Expected relative cost: low (~2–3 GPU hours), since singleprofile avoids the aggregation step entirely while still processing both modalities—cheaper than config_031 (3.60) and config_019 (4.82)."
}

